AB  - INTERVENTION: Behavioral : Experimental group : Tailored Activity Program (TAP) TAP is designed to adjust to the individual characteristics of patients and includes visiting occupational therapy, home‐based programs, and teletherapy. Based on the occupational profiles of patients, the requests of patients and caregivers were reflected, the goal activities were selected, and the occupational therapy was designed(total intervention 12 times = TAP program design 1 time + visiting the home 9 time + teletherapy 2 times). The intervention was performed by visiting the home of patients total of 9 times, twice a week, and 60 minutes per session. Participants were educated on the daily lives of dementia patients and the work simplification and environmental modification were performed. In fact, by performing goal activities with patients, the therapist expedited the performance through various methods such as verbal or sensory cues, feedback, and modeling. In order to make the goal activities as habits, repetitive training was conducted and training of caregivers for the home‐based program was performed. When visiting occupational therapy was not performed, the home‐based program was executed. In order to make the goal activities as habits, self‐training was performed. Task activities were implemented to enhance activity and restore work balance. By using checklists, the home‐based program was faithfully implemented. The checklist used items of Mini‐Dementia Care Assessment Packet (Mini‐DCAP). Total of two 20‐minute sessions of teletherapy was carried out. By talking on the phone with the caregivers, the therapist confirmed changes within the households and modified occupational therapy accordingly. Control group : General occupational therapy This study executed a total of 12 interventions, twice a week for six weeks, and 60 minutes per session. The control group performed general cognitive based occupational therapy combined with paper task and physical activity. CONDITION: Diseases of the nervous system PRIMARY OUTCOME: Behavioral Psychological Symptoms SECONDARY OUTCOME: Social Interactions INCLUSION CRITERIA: The targets of this research were dementia patients who are 65 or older, use daycare and visiting care services of a public health center, live at home with a caregiver, and have CDR(Clinical Dementia Rating Scale) score of 0.5~2 and MMSE‐K(Mini‐Mental State Examination‐Korean Version) score of 23 or less.
