AB  - Tested 2 hypotheses related to the effect of alcohol on memory: (1) the premature aging hypothesis and (2) the continuity hypothesis. Human subjects: 51 male and female West German adults. Six subgroups were formed: (1) alcoholics, recently detoxified; (2) alcoholics, detoxified 5 mo previously; (3) a control group matched to Groups 1 and 2; (4) Korsakoff patients; (5) Alcoholics Anonymous members; and (6) a control group matched to Groups 4 and 5. Ss were tested with the Leistungs-Prüf-System ('Achievement Testing System') by W. Horn (1962), a German version of the Wechsler Memory Scale (W. Böcher, 1963), and the symbol digit test from the German version of the Wechsler Adult Intelligence Scale (WAIS) ('HAWIE'). Ss then completed a task involving memorization of 20 orally-presented clusters of 4 words each. (German abstract) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
