AB  - The article presents the correlation of expectations, life satisfaction and diseases among the elderly from various social groups in Delhi, India. Particular focus is given to loneliness among the elders as a relative deficit in social relationship with others. Details related to the methods and random sampling to gather data on the subject are also discussed. Studies reveal significant correlation between expectation and the difference in actual treatment of various disease like depression, diabetes and hypertension are also discussed.
