AB  - In an investigation of research on technology to assist family members caring for a relative with dementia at home, the authors conducted research on five focus groups with 26 caregivers highlighted the question of whether intervention could or should be converted into a service. Caregivers concern for it their relatives with dementia highlighted at the concern for the safety, the lack of a comprehensive monitoring system, & the willingness to use technology although they weren't technology whizzes. Experimentation & evaluation of an off the shelf, Internet-based monitoring system indicates that training & maintenance of the system became bothersome, although some found that the system made their lives easier. This research experience indicates that the goal of providing caregivers with an "set it and forget it" technology system was unrealistic, although it is a potential resource when caring form a family member with certain stages of dementia. References. J. Harwell
