AB  - Evaluated the effects of a skills-building method developed to improve coping and social support networks of primary caregivers of children (aged 2–14 yrs) with developmental disabilities. 229 mothers and 1 grandmother participated in 1 of 2 intervention groups: a skills-building intervention or a comparison treatment intervention using traditional counseling methods. At posttest assessment, Ss in the skills-building sessions demonstrated improved coping and communication skills, greater satisfaction with social support networks, and a reduction in depression (Beck Depression Inventory) and stress levels. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
