AB  - Discusses therapeutic and management issues faced by outpatient clinicians working with Axis II personality disorder patients. These issues include (1) management and treatment of patients with both psychiatric and substance-abuse disorders; (2) the recurrent dangers these individuals pose to themselves and others; (3) the patients' intense demands for therapists to make active, extensive interventions and the impact this has on traditional therapist neutrality; (4) the patients' propensity for acting out anxiety and aggression and tendency to split clinicians and systems; and (5) countertransference responses experienced by practitioners. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
