AB  - Describes the methods, model, and typical problems of a psychosocial intervention for relatives of long-term mentally ill adults. The sample, assessment procedure, and evaluation of the intervention results were reported in another paper by B. MacCarthy et al (see record [rid]1989-40696-001[/rid]). Relatives were not selected for the group by patient diagnosis or motivation and little extra staff input was required. An interactive education session at home was followed by a monthly relatives' group which aimed to reduce components of expressed emotion (EE) and to alleviate their burden. The group facilitators adopted a directive but nonjudgmental style, and constructive coping efforts were encouraged. The intervention was effective at reducing EE and improving family relationships. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
