AB  - Investigated the course of illness among 95 male and 233 female schizophrenics seen in a public health service over a period of 2–10 yrs. Observations indicated a less promising prognosis, particularly with respect to the severity of symptoms, than that indicated by other clinical studies. Duration of the illness, social isolation, and size of the S's family were found to be unrelated to outcome. The relation of family illness history and sociocultural factors to outcome is discussed, and the effectiveness of long-term neuroleptic treatment in this group is described. (6 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
