AB  - Studied the effect of the relatives' school in a therapeutic community on the progress of 50 acute psychiatric inpatients (neurotics, psychotics, and alcoholics), 20 of whom served as control Ss. 100 families and the 30 experimental patients were interviewed, and 20 group sessions were held. Participation with relatives in group activity was found to have a beneficial effect on patients. A tendency to prefer mixed groups also was shown among relatives of patients. 88% of families and 76.6% of patients preferred mixed group activity. 96% of families and 70% of patients derived personal satisfaction from participating in mixed groups. Families that did not want to interact with patients complained that they could not speak freely in front of patients. Inclusion of patients' relatives in weekly programs in therapeutic communities is recommended. (English abstract) (13 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
