AB  - The purpose of this paper is to report findings from the first questionnaire used in the Women & Depression Project (WDP), & this paper is the first in a series of empirically based ones. The aim of WDP was threefold: (1) to develop a short-term therapeutic intervention in order to help & support marginalized, depressed women; (2) to generate an action research approach for depressed women; & (3) to gather valuable data concerning women's experiences of depression. WDP grew from the idea that a research framework modeled on feminist therapy can add to our knowledge about women & mental health. With both therapeutic & research aims, feminist therapy was utilized in group work with depressed women. The findings reveal the complexities of group members' lives & initial ideas on how members shaped their depression narratives. In this way, the paper starts to map out areas for further exploration & development about women who seek help for their depression in a self-help context.
