AB  - Evaluated the Psychosexual Treatment Program, a 35-wk community-based group treatment program for sex offenders, based on a cognitive-behavioral approach. Ss consisted of 35 offenders (25 pedophiles, 8 exhibitionists, and 2 paraphiliacs). An evaluation and a followup at 3, 6, and 12 mo indicates offenders gained and maintained significant treatment effects including a reduction in the frequency and arousal of deviant sexual fantasies, an increase in acceptance and control of their sexual problems, an enhancement of social and assertiveness skills, an improvement of sex knowledge, and a decrease of cognitive distortions associated with deviant sexual behaviors. Treatment efficacy, assessment of treatment needs, recidivism rates, the value of short-term evaluation, and drop-out rates are discussed. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
