AB  - The article discusses the 10 major characteristics of primary care mental health services, as provided by the Joint Commissioning Panel for Mental Health (JCP-MH). It says that mental health care must be patient-centred, in which patients are given time to talk about their care. It states that mental healthcare teams should have the skills and knowledge to offer the right treatment. Moreover, the services must be accessible through self-referral and should adjust to people with special needs.
