AB  - Presents data on the effects of combining methylphenidate (MTH) and fluoxetine (FLU) to treat 10 cocaine dependent outpatients. Only 4 of the 10 patients completed all 8 wks of treatment. Of the 6 who dropped out, 3 complained of increased cocaine craving that led to a severe cocaine binge after starting MTH. The combination of the drugs appeared to be detrimental in the treatment of this group of Ss. Only 1 of the 10 patients stopped using cocaine for any significant period; the authors suggest this single positive outcome was due to the positive effects of the drug combination on the patient's attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) rather than his drug addiction. The authors therefore caution against the use of the combination of MTH and FLU for treatment of cocaine-dependent patients without ADHD. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
