AB  - Examined opportunities and barriers to empowerment for people with severe mental illness through participation in treatment planning. 186 psychiatric hospital patients (average age 44 yrs) with severe mental illnesses, such as schizophrenia, personality disorders, substance abuse, and mental retardation, and their psychiatric hospital caregivers participated in focus groups. Focus group discussions concerned the development of treatment planning, participation in treatment planning, and barriers to effective and empowering treatment planning. Results show that barriers identified by Ss included limitations made by psychological disorders, mandatory core treatment activities, lack of choice of activities, lack of staff time allocated to treatment planning, and insufficient numbers of staff to escort clients to and from activities. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
