AB  - Examines how social work clinicians' exposure to focus groups positively alters research techniques & practical results. The analysis focused on clinicians from a crisis intervention center attached to a psychiatric emergency room in a large city, clients of which include a higher number of those dually diagnosed with mental disorder & substance abuse. Audiotaped sessions with clinicians, followed by analysis of the transcripts, showed that the focus groups successfully achieved two important results: (1) improved research questions that led to possible methods for a successful community service referral system for dually diagnosed clients, & (2) a heightened sense of responsibility in the research project that resulted in more intense recruitment of clients. 19 References. A. Durward
