AB  - The standard treatment for sexual disorders is multimodal, eclectic, and integrative. While no treatment program for the wide range of paraphilic and nonparaphilic "excessive sexual" disorders (e.g., compulsive or addictive) relies on pharmacotherapy alone to manage the complex issues, the role for antiandrogen treatment is widely accepted. In this paper I review the current status of antiandrogen treatment in order to begin a clinical dialogue to establish guidelines for a Standard of Care when prescribing antiandrogens for the treatment of sexual disorders. Issues, treatment options, other drug therapies, target groups, evaluation protocols, contraindications, side effects, improvement indices, and forensic issues are discussed. [ABSTRACT FROM AUTHOR] Copyright of Sexual Addiction & Compulsivity is the property of Routledge and its content may not be copied or emailed to multiple sites or posted to a listserv without the copyright holder's express written permission. However, users may print, download, or email articles for individual use. This abstract may be abridged. No warranty is given about the accuracy of the copy. Users should refer to the original published version of the material for the full abstract. (Copyright applies to all Abstracts.)
