AB  - Compared the functioning of 55 chronic psychotic patients (mean age 49.93) after they had received psychosocial treatment for nearly 5 yrs, with their functioning 3 mo after this treatment had been replaced with pharmacotherapy and custodial care. Results indicate that in only 3 mo, the removal of the therapeutic milieu, without any change in the patient–staff ratio, led to the deterioration of Ss' functioning. Patients deteriorated in all spheres, including psychotic symptomatology, psychotic behavior, anxiety, depression, withdrawal, social competence, social interest, and personal neatness. (11 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
