AB  - Assesses the impact of 10 culturally relevant indices of physical, psychological, & social functioning on the functional health of women diagnosed with osteoarthritis who have no known history of coexisting medical conditions that would cause severe debilitation. Multiple regression analysis of cross-sectional data obtained in face-to-face interviews with 100 older, low-income, community-living black women reveals that functional health is best explained by three interrelated variables: depression, timed eight-foot walk score, & number of arthritic joints. These findings emphasize the need for enhanced education of providers to stimulate development of health promotion/disease prevention programs that decrease the occurrence & effects of depression, physical immobility, & joint pathology. 2 Tables, 1 Figure, 49 References. Adapted from the source document.
