AB  - The article discuses how Doctor Mary Cesare-Murphy, executive director of Behavioral Health Care Accreditation for the Joint Commission, helped reform the agency's accreditation process. Topics discussed include how consumer inputs put a stop to abuse of restraints and seclusion of patients, and how it helped recognized treatment options beyond the hospital and integrated into primary care. Also discussed are the benefits of the agency's accreditation process to patients and providers. INSET: CARF and ACHC moving toward health homes, home care.
