AB  - Drawing on systemic theory, social psychology, & community psychology, a community-based family intervention model for drug dependency is proposed, suggesting that: drug dependence is a multifactoral process, prevention programs should be integrated into the broader context of health education, & desired changes in behavior can only be realized with the conscious involvement of community actors. The family is considered the basic unit of study & intervention within the community, especially its role in the socialization process of drug abuse prevention. A prevention program directed toward groups of parents, involving small group discussions & role playing, is described. 5 References. J. Taylor
