AB  - A report of an experimental research design that is being used in a demonstration project in Miami, Fla, to evaluate the effectiveness of AIDS (acquired immune deficiency syndrome) intervention programs among intravenous drug users (IVDUs) & their sexual partners. Components of the program include initial assessment, randomization into standard & enhanced intervention programs, & follow-up assessments at 6-month intervals. Results are reported here based on an experimental group of 335 who received enhanced treatment & a control group of 415 who received standard treatment. The findings suggest the effectiveness of the enhanced treatment, providing greater knowledge about AIDS transmission & prevention, especially with regard to needle sharing & safer sex practices. Despite the instability of these research Ss, all IVDUs, enhanced intervention had positive effects. 1 Table, 1 Figure, 7 References. J. W. Stanton
