AB  - Purpose. SMART Phone technology, such as the Addiction Comprehensive Health Enhancement Support System (ACHESS), provides a novel way to deliver personalized continuing care for AUD. Effective continuing care can also be delivered via Telephone Monitoring and Counseling (TMC). ACHESS and TMC have complementary strengths. ACHESS provides automated 24/7 recovery support services, but not regular contact with a counselor. TMC provides regular contact with a counselor, but no support between calls. The future of continuing care is likely to involve mobile technology and counselor contact, but little is known about how to integrate these services. The goal of the study was to determine whether adding TMC, ACHESS, and integrated TMC+ACHESS to intensive outpatient programs (IOP) improves substance use outcomes. Methods. Study featured a 2 x 2 design [ACHESS (yes/no) x TMC (yes/no)], in which 262 alcohol dependent patients were randomized after 3-4 weeks in IOP and followed up at 3, 6, 9, 12, and 18 months. Data on drinking was obtained with the Time-Line Follow-Back. Biological measures of drinking (GGT, CDT) were also obtained at baseline and 18 months. Data. Alcohol use at baseline and 3, 6, 9, and 12 months was analyzed for this abstract. Four main outcome measures were examined: Any drinking, any heavy drinking, % days any drinking, and % days heavy drinking. Data from the 18 month follow-up will also be included in the presentation. Results. Main effects favoring TMC were found on any drinking (p < .01), % days any drinking (p < .05), any heavy drinking (p < .04), and % days heavy drinking (p < .04). Main effects favoring ACHESS were found on % days any drinking (p < .04) and % days heavy drinking (p = .04). TMC and ACHESS did not differ. There were no significant TMC x ACHESS interactions, and none of the contrasts comparing TMC+ACHESS to TMC or ACHESS was significant. Conclusions. Results replicate prior findings that TMC and ACHESS are efficacious continuing care interventions, with approximately 50% reduction on measures of frequency of drinking compared to IOP only. However, the integrated TMC+ACHESS package did not improve outcomes over TMC or ACHESS provided separately.
