AB  - Describes an intervention designed to extinguish conditioned withdrawal and craving in former opiate addicts. Clinical outcome data from 35 outpatients on methadone maintenance indicate the following: (1) Conditioned withdrawal and craving were pervasive among both methadone-maintained Ss even though actual physical withdrawal was blocked and drug-free Ss even after 30 days of inpatient therapeutic community rehabilitation. (2) Conditioned withdrawal and craving were effectively extinguished in an intensive 3-wk inpatient procedure. (3) Emotional states such as anger, depression, and anxiety elicited and exacerbated conditioned withdrawal and craving and were an integral part of a conditioned stimulus (CS) complex. Problems associated with turning a laboratory-based procedure into a clinical intervention are noted. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
