AB  - Describes a group treatment for depression and withdrawal for a day-treatment population. 119 patients chose potentially pleasurable activities to engage in outside the center each week. Multiple imagery trials and group sharing were used to evoke and amplify pleasurable emotional responses. The procedure is presented in detail. According to self-reports, Ss responded with a 64% performance of new pleasurable activities and with an improved mood within the sessions. Results indicate that this kind of group intervention was influential in stimulating chronic patients with problems of withdrawal and depression into new activities that were experienced as pleasurable. Also, reportedly consistent elevations of global mood after sessions suggest some generalization to overall mood state. (9 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
