AB  - The article discusses rheumatoid arthritis (RA) as the most common inflammatory joint disorder affecting 690,000 people in Great Britain. It notes the association of RA with depression and the need for nurses in the community to help patients experiencing depression to re-engage with their care and treatment. RA is also associated with some complications like cardiovascular (CVD) disease and community nurses should be aware to screen patients with RA for CVD.
