AB  - Less than two weeks ago, a whirlwind of activity occurred among advocates and lawmakers around efforts to protect mental health and substance use disorder coverage. The American Psychological Association (APA), the National Association for Behavioral Healthcare, the Federation of American Hospitals, the National Association of Addiction Treatment Providers, and state attorneys general representing Connecticut, Illinois and Rhode Island have all taken action and submitted amicus briefs in order to reverse an overturned ruling in the landmark Wit v. United Behavioral Health (UBH) case. [ABSTRACT FROM AUTHOR] Copyright of Mental Health Weekly is the property of John Wiley & Sons, Inc. and its content may not be copied or emailed to multiple sites or posted to a listserv without the copyright holder's express written permission. However, users may print, download, or email articles for individual use. This abstract may be abridged. No warranty is given about the accuracy of the copy. Users should refer to the original published version of the material for the full abstract. (Copyright applies to all Abstracts.)
