AB  - Presents the results of discriminant analysis of persisters vs dropouts across 6 bulimia groups composed of 53 women (aged 18–48 yrs), 20 of whom dropped out prior to the 20th wk of therapy. The discriminant analysis was able to correctly classify dropouts and persisters 83% of the time on demographic variables, 73% of the time on tension and anxiety variables, and 90% of the time using cognitive variables. Dropouts were younger, unmarried, and unemployed and had less physical tension and more positive cognitive beliefs than persisters. Specific characteristics of persisters and dropouts and treatment implications are discussed. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
