AB  - Treated 41 hospitalized male depressive alcoholics (aged 25–67 yrs) for 6 yrs with the tetracyclic antidepressant mianserin. The average dose of mianserin was 50,7 mg/day either as a single dosage in the evening or 3–4 times per day. The minimum dosage was 30 mg/day, the maximum 120 mg/day. Withdrawal treatment was commenced as usual using clomethiazol. 28 patients showed lighting up of mood until discharge, as assessed by clinical impression. The authors note that mianserin is lacking anticholinergic effects. Therefore, neither exacerbation of a predelirant state nor the increased occurrence of epileptic seizures has to be feared. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
