AB  - Discusses crucial issues for the mother in the incest family during the middle phase of treatment. A conceptual framework useful in prioritizing these treatment issues is described. A successful treatment outcome requires the working through of the mother's feelings of stigmatization and sexual trauma. Group psychotherapy is emphasized as an important treatment modality, and an excerpt from the 24th session of a mothers' group is presented to illustrate how the key theoretical concepts manifest themselves in practice. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
