AB  - In a typical undergraduate Abnormal Psychology course, whether seated or online, diversity factors may be mentioned peripherally in textbook material or highlighted by an adept instructor. It is uncommon for course materials to discuss the implications of mental health research being centered on members of majority populations and what effect this might have on minority populations, especially those with multiple marginalized identities. This small group discussion activity shines a light on mental health considerations for marginalized populations, as well as discussing how intersections of those identities may affect mental health. This activity can also be tailored for online teaching or graduate courses in psychopathology and clinical judgment. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2021 APA, all rights reserved)
