AB  - If the reform of the mental health act is in any way indicative, the dominant view in the mass media and government seems to have shifted from a philosophy of welfare, treatment and care towards the Home Office agenda of public protection, confinement and indefinite exclusion. The issues raised by this reform tell as much about society's capacity for tolerance and cohesion as the future direction of services for the mentally ill.
