AB  - Ethnographic methods including participant observation & interviews with 40 intravenous drug users in various drug networks in the San Francisco & Los Angeles, Calif, areas were used to gather information concerning AIDS (acquired immune deficiency syndrome) knowledge & needle-sharing practices. R recommendations for AIDS education & intervention programs included: (1) make needles more available; (2) make drug treatment more available; (3) expand community health outreach worker-style programs (peer counseling); (4) create women-only groups, especially in drug treatment programs, to help empower women; & (5) use persons with AIDS who contracted it via IV drug use in informational campaigns, particularly on TV. Modified AA
