AB  - Mental illness stands among the leading causes of disease and disability in the world. We do not have the exact number of mental illness cases in the country, but estimates suggest that a higher rate of common mental illness is prevalent among women than men. Mental illness is a disability which impairs the well-being, optimal development and mental abilities and the person is not able to lead a normal life. Womens mental health is also determined by accessibility to mental health care, social support system, life events and gender stereotypes. In India, mental illness is still considered a manifestation of certain evil influences that possess the victim. [IBSSMB] Reprinted by permission of the Indian Social Institute, New Delhi
