AB  - The article presents a discussion about the management of trauma reactions in intensive addiction treatment environments. It explains that intensive addiction treatment environments present an outstanding opportunity to help trauma survivors with substance use disorders. Normally, such situations provide an array of group therapies, close monitoring by staff, and peers with whom to connect. However, it was just recently that trauma has become more accepted as a legitimate focus for work in addiction treatment.
