AB  - The article discusses research on the role of naltrexone and exposure therapy in treating alcohol dependence and post traumatic stress disorder (PTSD). It references a study by Edna B. Foa and colleagues in the August 7, 2013 issue of the "Journal of the American Medical Association." Eligible subjects were assigned to one of four treatment groups. The study found that all treatment participants had reduced PTSD symptoms but the main effect of prolonged exposure was said to be not significant.
