AB  - Analyzes the relationship between social capital, financial stressors, & religiosity, using data drawn from 200 interviews of randomly selected households in a high-poverty Birmingham, AL, residential community. A mediation model of well-being from a psychosocial resources approach to mental health is used to determine the significance & direction of the relationship between financial status & depression with religiosity & social capital as mediating factors. Given the dramatic growth of high poverty ghetto areas in the midst of a great American economic boom, this inquiry is important for policymakers & academic researchers.
